## 2. Extract Deeper Info Using aapt
Switch over to your target folder and run analytical commands to gather reconnaissance data:

cd ~/Downloads


* Find Deep Metadata & Entry Points:
Find the main entry launcher activity, targets, and SDK configurations:

aapt dump badging trust_wallet.apk

* Extract the Human-Readable Manifest:
Android binaries compress the XML. Use aapt to parse the structure out directly to a text file so you can search for exposed components, deep links, or intents:

aapt dump xmltree trust_wallet.apk AndroidManifest.xml > manifest_dump.txt

* Check for Hardcoded Asset Strings:
Look for embedded API configurations, local certificates, or encryption configurations stashed away inside the application assets:

aapt list trust_wallet.apk | grep -E "assets/|res/raw/"


