## 3. Read Code & Reverse Engineer
aapt is brilliant for metadata, but you cannot view source code logic with it. To do that, you need a reverse engineering tool chain on your Linux machine.
## Option A: Decompile directly to Java using JADX (Recommended)
JADX converts the compiled Dalvik bytecode (.dex files) directly into readable Java.

   1. Install JADX:
   
   sudo apt install jadx
   
   2. Open the APK visually:
   
   jadx-gui trust_wallet.apk
   
   This launches a graphical interface. You can click through package structures, use Ctrl+Shift+F to search for keywords like "http://", "secret", "private_key", or "api_key".

## Option B: Decode Resources using Apktool
If you want to modify the app, inject a proxy certificate, or look at layouts, you need apktool to unpack it into Smali assembly code.

   1. Install Apktool:
   
   sudo apt install apktool
   
   2. Unpack the APK:
   
   apktool d trust_wallet.apk -o decompiled_output_dir
   
   
